    "Trigger split reuses the existing CASE-003 credential without editing credential payloads",
    "Gate 5 never treats RUC/tax ID as authentication",
    "Gate 5 requires verified identity, active membership, invoice.read and resource ownership before invoice data is returned",
    "Gate 5 uses neutral NOT_FOUND_OR_NOT_AUTHORIZED for denied resource lookups",
    "Gate 5 audits every supplier invoice query",
    "Gate 5 has no outbound messaging node",
    "Gate 6 authenticates channel ingress before canonical data access",
    "Gate 6 uses provider_message_id replay protection per tenant and channel",
    "Gate 6 never treats RUC/tax ID as authentication and never auto-binds a channel identity from a RUC claim",
    "Gate 6 creates only pending verification requests against pre-existing trusted contact data",
    "Gate 6 masks trusted contact details and keeps verification delivery disabled",
    "Gate 6 has no outbound messaging node",
    "Gate 7 never trusts tenant_id from provider payloads; tenant scope resolves from a persisted provider/channel binding",
    "Gate 7 verifies Kapso HMAC-SHA256 and event/version/idempotency headers before business processing",
    "Gate 7 reuses existing HMAC and CASE-003 RPC credentials without editing credential payloads",
    "Gate 7 rejects invalid signatures before canonical data access",
    "Gate 7 fails closed with CONNECTOR_NOT_BOUND for unknown provider channel bindings",
    "Gate 7 preserves provider message replay safety and has no outbound messaging node",
    "Gate 8 proves a real user-originated WhatsApp message delivered by Kapso Cloud to CASE-003",
    "Gate 8 keeps CASE-002 live and unchanged while CASE-003 receives the same provider event in parallel",
    "Gate 8 returns AUTH_REQUIRED for an unverified real sender and does not disclose invoice data",
    "Gate 8 keeps CASE-003 outbound messaging disabled",
    "Gate 9 never treats RUC/tax ID as authentication",
    "Gate 9 stores only SHA-256 of verification codes and trusted-contact destinations",
    "Gate 9 limits challenge issuance per channel subject and supplier vendor",
    "Gate 9 requires trusted-contact code proof or explicit audited operator approval before identity binding",
    "Gate 9 creates invoice.read only after successful verification",
    "Gate 9 keeps email transport and WhatsApp outbound delivery separate from the identity core",
    "Gate 10 keeps challenge generation, expiry, attempts and verification authority in PostgreSQL",
    "Gate 10 uses native n8n Send Email with a dedicated SMTP credential",
    "Gate 10 test email overrides never modify SAP snapshot trusted-contact data",
    "Gate 10 test email overrides persist only a destination SHA-256 and masked destination",
    "Gate 10 never persists or logs the raw verification code outside the transient internal delivery payload"
